    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A four-bar house pattern whose fills run \"a few times\" rather than a fixed" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// number. `repeat 2 to 6 { … }` is the piece saying how long the figure may" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// run and leaving the rest to the performance — the same sentence a DJ writes" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// as \"loop until the cue lands\" and a folk singer writes as \"as many verses as" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// there are\"." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The count is chosen once, at compile time, from the realization" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// (`musa check examples/loop-lengths.musa --seed 42`). Everything below that" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// choice is an ordinary exact repeat, which is why the kernel gains nothing" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// from this file: see docs/rules/kernel/11-realization.md." },
